WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.010
A small firm can make up to 6 units.

2
00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.950
To sell more, it must cut its price.

3
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.330
Its revenue keeps climbing
all the way to the fifth unit,

4
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.240
where it peaks at 50.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.790
But its profit peaks sooner,

6
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.770
at just 3 units, at 16.

7
00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:18.630
The fourth and fifth units
still bring in money.

8
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.230
So why would a business
stop making more when

9
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.070
each extra sale still brings in money?

10
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.680
In this mission, you'll
build a profit table one

11
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.490
unit at a time and see where it turns.

12
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.920
Then you'll slide output
from 0 to 6 and hunt

13
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.900
for the top of the profit hill.

14
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.640
Your mission: find the
rule that tells a firm

15
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.390
exactly where to stop.
